  "body": "## Problem\n\nRuntime vector compound literals still used a private stack object after lowering: zero stores, scalar lane stores, and a whole-vector reload. This affected distinct integer lanes and zero tails in the lexer even when every byte was known and the object could not escape.\n\nCloses #3641.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Extend SROA's existing constant/splat recovery with complete runtime integer lanes (8/16/32/64-bit lanes; 16/32/64-byte vectors). Track each byte's latest store and accept a runtime lane only when that store is intact and aligned.\n- Reuse existing IR and backend rules: direct scalar widening for a low lane with a zero tail; otherwise independent 128-bit pieces combined by a balanced widening/insertion tree.\n- Preserve source SSA values and observable effects. Incomplete definitions, torn lanes, volatile construction accesses, escapes, and unsupported forms keep the memory path. Remove overlapping initialization stores only when every load of that private construction has been recovered.\n- Size remapped call metadata by call instructions, including valid IR that shares one descriptor across several calls; cover ordered side effects and live constants in a dedicated regression.\n- Enable the path in ordinary and inlined C bodies at AVX512F/BW/DQ/VL output targets, including `--tier1-passes=-inline`. Avoid the extra IR scan where the ordinary construction trigger cannot apply.\n- Add independent byte/effect oracles, actual strict Tier 1 report checks, conservative IR cases and assembly checks. Keep the existing scalar patterns at their original output target; compile the new constructors separately for Zen 5.\n\n## Validation\n\nBaseline: `74eacd4744a8131ba4c1a5bd8ad87b89ec0f7dbe`. Head: `3d48a78e9f6ee277c8d041022da296086c6a84f3`.\n\nBoth compilers built locally with the repository's pinned Clang 23.1.4, explicit vector host and Debug/`-g0`. These are correctness/code-shape checks on the cloud Xeon, not performance timings.\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `test-ir-inline` | 128,963 checks, 0 failures; frozen digest unchanged |\n| `test-ir-sroa` | 23,708 checks, 0 failures |\n| `test-ir-optimize` | 337,934 checks, 0 failures |\n| New IR matrix | 168 fixtures; 2,808 interpreter executions against independent expected bytes, plus a shared-call-descriptor regression |\n| Strict native constructors | All four existing-mode × inline-on/off combinations pass; 897 byte comparisons per run plus side-effect checks |\n| Tier 1 selection | 15/15 constructors compiled/certified with one inline expansion; 16/16 with inlining disabled; zero fallbacks |\n| Existing patterns | Original 38 functions and shape checks pass |\n| #3311 register aggregates | 32 functions, interpreter and both strict native paths pass; retained assembly checks pass |\n| Lower-target compatibility probe | Four runtime construction forms, 256 byte checks each with Clang/base/head at x86-64-v3; base/head objects identical |\n\nThe exact baseline passes the byte/effect oracles but fails precisely nine new construction shape checks. Head removes the construction memory traffic:\n\n| Constructor | Baseline stack accesses | Head stack accesses |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Single scalar + zero tail | 10 | 0 |\n| Alternating scalars | 17 | 0 |\n| Inlined two-scalar helper + zero tail | 11 | 0 |\n| Mixed constants/scalars | 17 | 0 |\n| Eight distinct inputs | 17 | 2* |\n| First/last runtime lanes | 17 | 0 |\n| 8/16/32-bit lane forms | 13 each | 0 each |\n\n\\* The eight-distinct-input case has one matched save/reload of the **output pointer**, verified at the same stack address and consumed by the sole output vector store. It has no construction-lane stack stores or vector stack reload. Every other pure constructor requires zero stack accesses.\n\nThe focused x86-64-v3 probe passes. The broader constructor unit also encounters an existing splat vector-splitting refusal on both baseline and head; their diagnostics are identical, so this PR does not claim that broader unit passes on v3.\n\nRaw logs, assembly, command/provenance records and the lower-target probe are being published to `buster14a/buster-performance/docs/measurements/tier1-runtime-vector-construction-3641-2026-11-26`; a pinned link will be added after publication. Standard hosted PR CI is the remaining validation. No 9700X access, benchpress job, or hardware dispatch was requested or started.\n\n## Provenance\n\nOriginal implementation and tests; no third-party implementation was imported. Clang is an external oracle. All three commits carry the maintainer's authorized DCO trailer.\n\n---\nAgent session: 6b081363-0e34-83ed-a298-c8acc059b07f (OpenAI session ID; no share URL is exposed)\nContributing agent threads: 6b0813c5-7aa0-83ed-a3e8-af56a4a38052; 6b0813cf-d8bc-83ed-84cc-51368a9a8056; 6b0813d9-dc64-83ed-846b-d9c5df1cb042 (no share URLs are exposed)\nModel: OpenAI / GPT-6 Astra Pro (all contributing agents)\n",
